; raster -- VU1 microprogram, uploaded from VIDMARasterMicrocode (0x004E5880).
; Generated by vudis.py extract; `vudis.py check` assembles it back
; against the SUPPORT image.  One line per instruction pair, upper first.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; VU1 DATA MEMORY, as the EE writes it (decomp/src/viraster.cpp)
;
;   0..20   the per-frame uniform block, UploadMatrices (UNPACK V4-32 NUM 21 at
;           0, then MSCAL VIRInit).  SPR 0x70000000 is its source:
;     0- 3  model->screen   SPR+0x140 = (modelView * projection) * clipToScreen
;     4- 7  model->clip     SPR+0x080 = modelView * projection
;     8-11  clip->screen    SPR+0x0C0 (uploaded, NOT loaded by VIRInit)
;     12    sun direction in MODEL space, (x, -z, y, 0)        SPR+0x180
;     13    point light position in model space, w = 1/range   SPR+0x190, +0x1CC
;     14    (m_p45C8 as an INT, SPR+0x22C, 0, SPR+0x228)
;     15    sun colour, or 0 when SPR+0x221 is clear           SPR+0x1AC
;     16    point light colour, or 0 when SPR+0x222 is clear   SPR+0x1D0
;     17    ambient, or 0 when SPR+0x220 is clear              SPR+0x1E0
;           -- REPLACED per material by UploadPerMaterial (ambient + the sun
;           tint quantised at SPR+0x224), then MSCAL VIRMaterial
;     18    the four unpack scales of a PACKED prim buffer     SPR+0x210..0x21C
;     19    fog (scale, offset, near clamp, far clamp)         SPR+0x1F0
;     20    static lighting colour                             SPR+0x200
;   435..   a GIF packet area: a count, then packets XGKICKed from 436 on
;           (the billboard program kicks 437 too)
;   612..   the skinning palette, VIMatrix44 x n, from SetObjectBlends
;           (ObjectBlendsBuffer); a bone index i reads 612 + 4*i
;   932..   the 32 pre-translations, from UploadPreTrans (PreTransBuffer);
;           a VIRStrip3 vertex's pos.w indexes them
;   ..1023  a STACK, vi15, growing down from 1024 (VIRInit sets it)
;   the vertex input arrives through the VIF double buffer (BASE/OFFSET from
;   UploadRasterMicro: PrimBuffer1, PrimBuffer2) and is found with XTOP.
;
; REGISTERS VIRInit leaves resident across calls
;   vf01-vf04 model->screen    vf05-vf08 model->clip
;   vf09 sun dir   vf10 point pos / 1/range   vf11 qword 14
;   vf12 sun colour   vf13 point colour   vf14 ambient (+ material tint)
;   vf29 pack scales   vf30 fog   vf31 static lighting (the fan path reuses
;   vf31 as a scratch clip position, so it is resident only for the strips
;   that do not)        vi15 the stack pointer
;
; ENTRY POINTS, and who MSCALs them (viraster.cpp, viprimbuffer.cpp End(),
; vicolorbuffer.cpp Color())
;   VIRInit      0  UploadMatrices -- latches the uniform block into registers
;   VIRMaterial 22  UploadPerMaterial -- reloads vf14 only
;   VIRFan      26  EndTriFan, BlitEnd (immediate mode and 2D) -- READ AND VERIFIED
;                   (spec_strip.py 'fan'): the strip loop with vertex 0 pinned
;                   (vf18/vf15/vi04), parity vi09 fixed at 32, clip via clip_fan
;   VIRStrip   317  EndTriStrip; VIPrimBufferTypeVUNC (unpacked V4-32)
;   VIRStrip2  429  VIPrimBufferTypePackVUNC; VIColorBuffer's baked colours
;                   (vf11.x == 0, point light out of reach: strip2_unlit)
;   VIRStrip3  549  VIPrimBufferTypePackVUNCG (positions + a pre-translation)
;   VIRStrip4  668  VIPrimBufferTypePackVUNBW -- the SKINNING pre-pass: unpacks,
;                   blends four palette matrices per vertex, rewrites the
;                   vertices in VUNC layout and `b VIRStrip`
;   VIRStrip5  807  DrawPrimBufferTessPackVUNCG (the tessellator's output) -- READ
;                   ('strip5'): float vertices, lit as VIRStrip3, not pipelined
;   VIRStrip6  924  VIPrimBufferTypePackVU -- READ ('strip6'): position + (s,t,q)
;                   only; colour amb + sunC*k + ptC*falloff*k, k = vf11.y, a = vf11.w
;   1037..2028      shared code, reached by BAL (link vi12 or vi14):
;     layer_emitter  the LAYER EMITTER: walks the list at 435 (count, then one
;            entry per material layer), XGKICKs each layer's A+D GS-state
;            packet (437 on), builds its GIF packet at 539 (PRIM 0x3C:
;            fogged, textured, gouraud strip; REGS ST, RGBAQ, XYZF2; NLOOP N)
;            and converts the 142+ buffer into it through the jump table at
;            1075 (jr vi10), one routine per pass type: 0 solid layer_solid,
;            1 textured/wrap layer_tex_wrap, 2 wire layer_wire (lines, NLOOP (N-2)*4+1,
;            template +12; the special case at 1051), 3 textured/clamp layer_tex_clamp
;            (all four routines READ AND VERIFIED: spec_layer.py; 0 solid and
;            2 wire from the forced captures solid.bin / wire.bin)
;     THE CLIPPER -- READ AND VERIFIED (spec_clip.py, test_spec_clip.py):
;     clip_strip  (strips; clip_fan is the fans' copy) spills vf15-vf28/vi01-vi14, puts
;            the triangle at 214 as a CLOSED polygon, 5 qwords a vertex: header
;            (x clip code, y 0 = original / 1 = made), clip pos, STQ, RGBA,
;            screen; order n-2,n-1,n,n-2, reversed when parity vi09 != vi10
;            (fans: hub,n-1,n,hub); BAL clip_polygon with vi09 = 3; draws the result
;            through layer_emitter as a FAN (vi03 = 1); restores and returns
;     clip_polygon  Sutherland-Hodgman, planes z+ z- x+ x- y+ y- (bits 16 32 1 2 4 8)
;            where vi07 (the union of codes, grown by made vertices) has the
;            bit; vf23.x = -1 / +1 is the side, vi01 the axis routine (1761 x,
;            1784 y, 1807 z); buffers 214 / 264 ping-pong (clip_swap swaps and
;            takes the new count); an empty pass returns vi11 = 0; clip_to_screen last
;     clip_plane_pass  one plane: per edge (prev, cur), copy an inside prev, add the
;            intersection of a crossing edge (clip_intersect -> jr vi01), close the
;            output with a copy of its first vertex
;     1761.. the intersection: d = c + s*w at both ends; interpolate FROM the
;            end the sign of (prev.c - cur.c) picks (the sub's MAC flag, four
;            cycles before fmand); t by DIV; lerp clip pos, STQ, RGBA; the
;            screen qword is left stale; new code, y = 1, ORed into vi07
;     clip_to_screen  the result in the 142 layout at the other buffer: made vertices
;            projected through qwords 8-11, STQ.z = 1/w (the lerped q is
;            dropped), fog = lerped STQ.w; fan-triangle backface cull from the
;            second vertex (the second tests against a STALE vf27)
;     1346, 1351-1353 and 183-186 (VIRFan) are unreachable: after a b / jr, and
;            clip_fan jumps back into the fan loop instead of returning
;     1968..2028  UNREACHABLE: no branch or entry reaches it (after jr vi14).
;            A register dump to 100+ ending [e], then lq vf30, N(vi01) for N =
;            21 314 435 612 932 964 -- the data map's boundaries, as code
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

